-+# Task 1 result
-+
-+## Changed
-+
-+- `crates/core/Cargo.toml`: added `[dependencies]` with `serde` and
-+  `serde_json`, both `workspace = true`, and nothing else.
-+- `crates/core/src/lib.rs`: declared `pub mod event` and re-exported
-+  `Event`, `Envelope`, `EventError`, `Nullable`, `parse_event_line`,
-+  `event_line`.
-+- `crates/core/src/event.rs`: module root; declares the submodules and
-+  re-exports the public surface.
-+- `crates/core/src/event/payload.rs`: one struct per row of "Event types"
-+  (35 types), required fields plain, optional fields `Option`, `or null`
-+  fields `Nullable`, nested objects and arrays of objects `serde_json::Value`,
-+  decimal-capable numbers (`duration`, `cost`, `durationSeconds`,
-+  `elapsedSeconds`) `serde_json::Number`. Every struct is
-+  `deny_unknown_fields` with `rename_all = "camelCase"` and
-+  `skip_serializing_if` on optional fields, so absence stays absence.
-+- `crates/core/src/event/nullable.rs`: `Nullable<T>` distinguishes absent,
-+  `null` and a value, as `Option` alone cannot.
-+- `crates/core/src/event/model.rs`: the `Event` enum with one variant per
-+  type, serialized adjacently as `type`/`data`, plus the match that reads a
-+  payload from its type name and yields `UnknownType` for a name not in the
-+  table.
-+- `crates/core/src/event/error.rs`: `EventError` with `NotJson`,
-+  `InvalidEnvelope`, `UnknownType(String)` and `InvalidData(String)`, with
-+  `Display` and `Error`.
-+- `crates/core/src/event/line.rs`: `Envelope`, `parse_event_line` (two-step:
-+  object and exact keys first, then typed data) and `event_line`.
-+- `crates/core/tests/events.rs`: proves every-event-type-parses,
-+  absent-null-and-numbers-stay-as-written and lines-that-are-refused.
-+- `crates/core/tests/no_io.rs`: proves core-source-names-no-io-module by
-+  reading the manifest's `[dependencies]` and every `.rs` under `src/`.
-+- `crates/core/tests/event_corpus.rs`: proves archived-event-logs-round-trip
-+  over every `.run/events/*.jsonl` under `openspec/changes/archive/`, naming
-+  file, line and error on failure and failing when it finds no event file.
-+- `Cargo.lock`: written by the first build (fetches `serde`, `serde_json` and
-+  their transitive crates).
-+
-+Both gates pass: `cargo test -p osq-core --test events --test event_corpus
-+--test no_io` (the round-trip test walks all 79,367 archived lines) and
-+`sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` (fmt check, `clippy --workspace --all-targets -D
-+warnings`, `cargo test --workspace`).
